The MinGW page pointed me to http://www.projectpluto.com/win32a.htm, a port of
PDCurses to Win32.  I'm presently testing NetHack-i18n linked against it, and it
may be of interest to the other variants that support the Curses interface.

My motive for using this is that NetHack-i18n needs wide character support,
which PDCurses for SDL does not have.  I got fairly good results using PDCurses
for the Win32 console, but it has the limitations of the console:  most
relevantly, underline shows up as deep blue.  Win32a shows a proper underline.

A further advantage is that a Curses interface for Win32 can be built without
the SDL library.  I suppose it could also coexist with a full windowed port,
such as the existing Win32 port, in a single binary; I have not tried to build
such a binary.

The one problem I've yet observed is that I once got a segfault from maximizing
the window.  I have not been able to make this happen a second time and I don't
know what happened -- it could be my fault for all I know.

It is limited to the Courier font.  According to the developer, the others don't
properly support both bold and italic.  I suspect he might be doing something
wrong.



